---Impala server linked service properties.
---@class azure.datafactory.ImpalaLinkedServiceTypeProperties
---@field host any The IP address or host name of the Impala server. (i.e. 192.168.222.160)
---@field port? any The TCP port that the Impala server uses to listen for client connections. The default value is 21050.
---@field authenticationType azure.datafactory.ImpalaAuthenticationType|string The authentication type to use.
---@field username? any The user name used to access the Impala server. The default value is anonymous when using SASLUsername.
---@field password? azure.datafactory.SecretBase The password corresponding to the user name when using UsernameAndPassword.
---@field thriftTransportProtocol? azure.datafactory.ImpalaThriftTransportProtocol|string The transport protocol to use in the Thrift layer (for V2 only). Default value is Binary.
---@field enableSsl? any Specifies whether the connections to the server are encrypted using SSL. The default value is false.
---@field enableServerCertificateValidation? any Specify whether to enable server SSL certificate validation when you connect.Always use System Trust Store (for V2 only). The default value is true.
---@field trustedCertPath? any The full path of the .pem file containing trusted CA certificates for verifying the server when connecting over SSL. This property can only be set when using SSL on self-hosted IR. The default value is the cacerts.pem file installed with the IR.
---@field useSystemTrustStore? any Specifies whether to use a CA certificate from the system trust store or from a specified PEM file. The default value is false.
---@field allowHostNameCNMismatch? any Specifies whether to require a CA-issued SSL certificate name to match the host name of the server when connecting over SSL. The default value is false.
---@field allowSelfSignedServerCert? any Specifies whether to allow self-signed certificates from the server. The default value is false.
---@field encryptedCredential? string The encrypted credential used for authentication. Credentials are encrypted using the integration runtime credential manager. Type: string.

