---MariaDB server linked service properties.
---@class azure.datafactory.MariaDBLinkedServiceTypeProperties
---@field driverVersion? any The version of the MariaDB driver. Type: string. V1 or empty for legacy driver, V2 for new driver. V1 can support connection string and property bag, V2 can only support connection string. The legacy driver is scheduled for deprecation by October 2024.
---@field connectionString? any An ODBC connection string. Type: string, SecureString or AzureKeyVaultSecretReference.
---@field server? any Server name for connection. Type: string.
---@field port? any The port for the connection. Type: integer.
---@field username? any Username for authentication. Type: string.
---@field database? any Database name for connection. Type: string.
---@field sslMode? any This option specifies whether the driver uses TLS encryption and verification when connecting to MariaDB. E.g., SSLMode=<0/1/2/3/4>. Options: DISABLED (0) / PREFERRED (1) (Default) / REQUIRED (2) / VERIFY_CA (3) / VERIFY_IDENTITY (4), REQUIRED (2) is recommended to only allow connections encrypted with SSL/TLS.
---@field useSystemTrustStore? any This option specifies whether to use a CA certificate from the system trust store, or from a specified PEM file. E.g. UseSystemTrustStore=<0/1>; Options: Enabled (1) / Disabled (0) (Default)
---@field password? azure.datafactory.AzureKeyVaultSecretReference The Azure key vault secret reference of password in connection string.
---@field encryptedCredential? string The encrypted credential used for authentication. Credentials are encrypted using the integration runtime credential manager. Type: string.

