---@class azure.datafactory.PhoenixLinkedServiceTypeProperties
---@field host any The IP address or host name of the Phoenix server. (i.e. 192.168.222.160)
---@field port? any The TCP port that the Phoenix server uses to listen for client connections. The default value is 8765.
---@field httpPath? any The partial URL corresponding to the Phoenix server. (i.e. /gateway/sandbox/phoenix/version). The default value is hbasephoenix if using WindowsAzureHDInsightService.
---@field authenticationType azure.datafactory.PhoenixAuthenticationType|string The authentication mechanism used to connect to the Phoenix server.
---@field username? any The user name used to connect to the Phoenix server.
---@field password? azure.datafactory.SecretBase The password corresponding to the user name.
---@field enableSsl? any Specifies whether the connections to the server are encrypted using SSL. The default value is false.
---@field trustedCertPath? any The full path of the .pem file containing trusted CA certificates for verifying the server when connecting over SSL. This property can only be set when using SSL on self-hosted IR. The default value is the cacerts.pem file installed with the IR.
---@field useSystemTrustStore? any Specifies whether to use a CA certificate from the system trust store or from a specified PEM file. The default value is false.
