---Spark Server linked service properties.
---@class azure.datafactory.SparkLinkedServiceTypeProperties
---@field host any IP address or host name of the Spark server
---@field port any The TCP port that the Spark server uses to listen for client connections.
---@field serverType? azure.datafactory.SparkServerType|string The type of Spark server.
---@field thriftTransportProtocol? azure.datafactory.SparkThriftTransportProtocol|string The transport protocol to use in the Thrift layer.
---@field authenticationType azure.datafactory.SparkAuthenticationType|string The authentication method used to access the Spark server.
---@field username? any The user name that you use to access Spark Server.
---@field password? azure.datafactory.SecretBase The password corresponding to the user name that you provided in the Username field
---@field httpPath? any The partial URL corresponding to the Spark server.
---@field enableSsl? any Specifies whether the connections to the server are encrypted using SSL. The default value is false.
---@field enableServerCertificateValidation? any Specifies whether the connections to the server will validate server certificate, the default value is True. Only used for Version 2.0
---@field trustedCertPath? any The full path of the .pem file containing trusted CA certificates for verifying the server when connecting over SSL. This property can only be set when using SSL on self-hosted IR. The default value is the cacerts.pem file installed with the IR.
---@field useSystemTrustStore? any Specifies whether to use a CA certificate from the system trust store or from a specified PEM file. The default value is false.
---@field allowHostNameCNMismatch? any Specifies whether to require a CA-issued SSL certificate name to match the host name of the server when connecting over SSL. The default value is false.
---@field allowSelfSignedServerCert? any Specifies whether to allow self-signed certificates from the server. The default value is false.
---@field encryptedCredential? string The encrypted credential used for authentication. Credentials are encrypted using the integration runtime credential manager. Type: string.

