---SQL Server linked service properties.
---@class azure.datafactory.SqlServerLinkedServiceTypeProperties
---@field server? any The name or network address of the instance of SQL Server to which to connect, used by recommended version. Type: string (or Expression with resultType string).
---@field database? any The name of the database, used by recommended version. Type: string (or Expression with resultType string).
---@field encrypt? any Indicate whether TLS encryption is required for all data sent between the client and server, used by recommended version. Possible values are true/yes/mandatory, false/no/optional and strict. Type: string (or Expression with resultType string).
---@field trustServerCertificate? any Indicate whether the channel will be encrypted while bypassing walking the certificate chain to validate trust, used by recommended version. Type: Boolean (or Expression with resultType boolean).
---@field hostNameInCertificate? any The host name to use when validating the server certificate for the connection. When not specified, the server name from the Data Source is used for certificate validation, used by recommended version. Type: string (or Expression with resultType string).
---@field applicationIntent? any The application workload type when connecting to a server, used by recommended version. Possible values are ReadOnly and ReadWrite. Type: string (or Expression with resultType string).
---@field connectTimeout? any The length of time (in seconds) to wait for a connection to the server before terminating the attempt and generating an error, used by recommended version. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field connectRetryCount? any The number of re-connections attempted after identifying that there was an idle connection failure, used by recommended version. This must be an integer between 0 and 255. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field connectRetryInterval? any The amount of time (in seconds) between each re-connection attempt after identifying that there was an idle connection failure, used by recommended version. This must be an integer between 1 and 60. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field loadBalanceTimeout? any The minimum time, in seconds, for the connection to live in the connection pool before being destroyed, used by recommended version. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field commandTimeout? any The default wait time (in seconds) before terminating the attempt to execute a command and generating an error, used by recommended version. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field integratedSecurity? any Indicate whether User ID and Password are specified in the connection (when false) or whether the current Windows account credentials are used for authentication (when true), used by recommended version. Type: Boolean (or Expression with resultType boolean).
---@field failoverPartner? any The name or address of the partner server to connect to if the primary server is down, used by recommended version. Type: string (or Expression with resultType string).
---@field maxPoolSize? any The maximum number of connections allowed in the connection pool for this specific connection string, used by recommended version. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field minPoolSize? any The minimum number of connections allowed in the connection pool for this specific connection string, used by recommended version. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field multipleActiveResultSets? any When true, an application can maintain multiple active result sets (MARS). When false, an application must process or cancel all result sets from one batch before it can execute any other batch on that connection, used by recommended version. Type: Boolean (or Expression with resultType boolean).
---@field multiSubnetFailover? any If your application is connecting to an AlwaysOn availability group (AG) on different subnets, setting MultiSubnetFailover=true provides faster detection of and connection to the (currently) active server, used by recommended version. Type: Boolean (or Expression with resultType boolean).
---@field packetSize? any The size in bytes of the network packets used to communicate with an instance of server, used by recommended version. Type: integer (or Expression with resultType integer).
---@field pooling? any Indicate whether the connection will be pooled or explicitly opened every time that the connection is requested, used by recommended version. Type: Boolean (or Expression with resultType boolean).
---@field connectionString? any The connection string. Type: string, SecureString or AzureKeyVaultSecretReference.
---@field authenticationType? azure.datafactory.SqlServerAuthenticationType|string The type used for authentication. Type: string.
---@field userName? any The on-premises Windows authentication user name. Type: string (or Expression with resultType string).
---@field password? azure.datafactory.SecretBase The on-premises Windows authentication password.
---@field encryptedCredential? string The encrypted credential used for authentication. Credentials are encrypted using the integration runtime credential manager. Type: string.
---@field alwaysEncryptedSettings? azure.datafactory.SqlAlwaysEncryptedProperties Sql always encrypted properties.
---@field credential? azure.datafactory.CredentialReference The credential reference containing authentication information.

